course: dictionary
lesson: 14749
title: Grand announcements
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A pronouncement is a formal statement. It is a serious way of saying something, often to announce a decision that has already been made.
explain: «The mayor made a pronouncement that the school would close early on Friday.» The clues are made and would close. The mayor is telling everyone about a decision, so a pronouncement is an official announcement.
explain: Sometimes a pronouncement is said in a grand, bossy way, as if people must obey it. «Her pronouncement, "Nobody leaves until the room is tidy!", made everyone groan.» The word grand and the bossy tone show it is an order, not a question.
fact: Pronouncement is a noun. Its plural is pronouncements.
fact: «Pronouncement» means a formal or official statement, often one that announces a decision.
fact: «Pronouncement» can also mean a grand statement that people feel they must obey.
fact: Kings, judges and governments often make pronouncements, in history and in the news.
fact: The Queen of Hearts's «Off with her head!» is a famous pronouncement in Alice in Wonderland.
exercise: «The mayor's pronouncement said the park would stay open all night.» What is a pronouncement? | *A formal statement announcing a decision | A long walk in the rain | A kind of park with lots of trees | A small whisper between friends
exercise: The judge read out her pronouncement in court. What does this tell you? | She was singing a song | She lost her glasses | She fell asleep in court | *She made an official announcement of her decision
exercise: Which of these is a pronouncement? | «We played football after lunch.» | «The cat slept on the mat.» | «It was a sunny day.» | *«The king declared that all schools would close on Monday.»
test: «The headteacher made a pronouncement: sports day is cancelled.» What does pronouncement mean? | A list of school rules to copy | A game played outside | A loud noise in the hall | *A formal announcement of a decision
test: Which word is closest in meaning to pronouncement? | whisper | *announcement | picnic | question
exam: «The queen's pronouncement was read aloud in every village.» What does pronouncement mean here? | A small noise made by a bird | A fast game played in the street | A picture hung on a wall | *A formal, official statement that announces a decision
